What:		/proc/jank_info/cpu_jank_info/callstack
Date:		September 2026
KernelVersion:	4.14.357-openela-miru-h40
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read-only ColorOS 14 task-stall call-stack feed.  Each populated
		record uses the OnePlus 9R grammar:

		[realtime_seconds.realtime_nanoseconds] [pid] [symbol<-symbol]

		The feed retains at most 64 records and up to four kernel frames per
		record.  A record is captured only when one of the four explicitly
		selected task_track PIDs leaves a non-I/O uninterruptible sleep that
		lasted at least 50 ms.  task_track_enable must be nonzero, so the
		producer and its existing sched_switch/sched_waking tracepoints are
		absent from the normal scheduling path.

		H.40 uses its native CONFIG_STACKTRACE task walker while the waking
		task still has a saved non-running context.  Storage is a fixed static
		ring.  This ABI adds no Binder, Futex, scheduler-tick, or dynamically
		allocated capture path.  A read before any qualifying stall returns
		<NULL>; a read while task tracking is disabled returns the donor's
		disabled message.
Users:		ColorOS performance diagnostics compatible with the OnePlus 9R
		Android 14 CPU-jank ABI.
